                <note rend="inline" type="source">Pauley
                    Files</note>
                <head>No. 876<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States Delegation Working
                        Paper</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">?</hi>]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-23">Undated</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 19</p>
                <p>Payment of reparations should leave sufficient resources to enable the German
                    people to subsist without external assistance.</p>
                <p>Payment for imports into Germany approved by the Control Council shall be a first
                    charge against the proceeds of exports out of current production and out of
                    stocks of goods.</p>
                <p>If the Control Council fails to agree, each zone commander may still import into
                    his own zone such supplies as his Government considers essential, for the
                    payment of which he may assess a first charge on exports of current production
                    and stocks from his own zone.</p>
            </div>
